window.DD_TESTS = [{"exam":"sat","set":1,"title":{"en":"SAT Reading and Writing — Practice module 1","th":"SAT Reading and Writing — ชุดฝึก 1"},"note":{"en":"One 27-question module in Digital SAT format. DeepDistrict practice — not an official College Board test.","th":"1 โมดูล 27 ข้อ รูปแบบ Digital SAT — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการของ College Board"},"minutes":32,"kinds":{"sat":27},"subjects":{},"free":true,"file":"sat-1","sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"e","passage":"Nang yai, a form of Thai shadow theatre, uses large panels of carved leather that performers hold above their heads while they dance in front of a lit screen. Because a single panel can weigh several kilograms and a performance may last for hours, the dancers must be physically ______.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["ornate","fragile","hesitant","robust"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The dancers carry heavy panels for hours, so they must be strong and able to endure: 'robust'. 'Fragile' is the opposite, 'hesitant' describes uncertainty rather than physical strength, and 'ornate' describes decoration, not a person's body.","th":"นักแสดงต้องถือแผ่นหนังหนักหลายกิโลกรัมเป็นเวลาหลายชั่วโมง จึงต้องแข็งแรงทนทาน คือ robust ส่วน fragile (เปราะบาง) มีความหมายตรงข้าม hesitant (ลังเล) ไม่เกี่ยวกับร่างกาย และ ornate (ประดับประดา) ใช้กับสิ่งของ ไม่ใช่ความแข็งแรงของคน"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"e","passage":"Bangkok was once known as the \"Venice of the East\" because so many of its residents travelled and traded along canals, called khlongs. During the twentieth century, many khlongs were filled in to make room for roads as the city grew. In recent years, several districts have begun cleaning and reopening sections of canal for boat services and to help drain water during heavy rain.","stem":"Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To compare Bangkok's canals in detail with those of Venice","To argue that Bangkok should replace its roads with canals","To describe how the role of Bangkok's canals has changed over time","To explain how the boats used on Bangkok's canals are built"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The text moves from the past (canals as main routes), to the twentieth century (canals filled in), to the present (canals reopened), so it describes how their role has changed. It never argues for removing roads, mentions Venice only in a nickname, and says nothing about how boats are built.","th":"ข้อความเล่าจากอดีต (คลองเป็นเส้นทางหลัก) สู่ศตวรรษที่ 20 (คลองถูกถมเป็นถนน) และปัจจุบัน (เปิดคลองใหม่) จึงเป็นการอธิบายว่าบทบาทของคลองเปลี่ยนไปอย่างไร ข้อความไม่ได้เสนอให้รื้อถนน ไม่ได้เปรียบเทียบกับเวนิสอย่างละเอียด และไม่ได้พูดถึงการสร้างเรือ"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"m","passage":"Hummingbirds use energy faster than almost any other animal of their size, and they must feed every few minutes during the day. At night, when they cannot feed, this might seem to put them at risk of running out of energy before dawn. The birds avoid this danger by entering torpor, a state in which their body temperature and heart rate drop sharply, greatly reducing the energy they burn while they rest.","stem":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It traces the history of a discovery and then predicts what scientists will learn next.","It describes an experiment on an animal and then points out a weakness in the method.","It identifies a challenge that an animal faces and then explains how the animal deals with it.","It presents two theories about an animal's behaviour and then rejects both of them."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The text first sets up a problem (hummingbirds burn energy fast and cannot feed at night) and then gives the solution (torpor). No theories are rejected, no experiment or method is described, and there is no history of a discovery or prediction.","th":"ข้อความเริ่มด้วยปัญหา (นกฮัมมิงเบิร์ดใช้พลังงานเร็วและกินอาหารตอนกลางคืนไม่ได้) แล้วอธิบายวิธีแก้ (เข้าสู่ภาวะ torpor) ข้อความไม่ได้เสนอทฤษฎีสองแบบ ไม่ได้บรรยายการทดลองหรือจุดอ่อนของวิธีการ และไม่ได้เล่าประวัติการค้นพบหรือทำนายอนาคต"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"evidence-textual","difficulty":"e","passage":"Every evening, thousands of fireflies gather in the mangrove trees along a river in Samut Songkhram province, flashing in the dark. A team of ecologists has hypothesized that bright artificial light from riverside buildings reduces the number of fireflies that gather in nearby trees.","stem":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support the ecologists' hypothesis?","choices":["Tourist boats travelled along the river more often on weekends than on weekdays.","The number of fireflies was about the same in trees near lit buildings and in trees far from them.","Mangrove trees growing next to buildings were taller than those growing farther away.","Trees far from lit buildings hosted many more fireflies than trees of the same species growing next to lit buildings."],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The hypothesis predicts fewer fireflies near artificial light. A finding that trees far from lit buildings had many more fireflies than similar trees near them fits that prediction. Equal numbers near and far would weaken the hypothesis, while boat traffic and tree height say nothing about light and firefly numbers.","th":"สมมติฐานคาดว่าแสงไฟจากอาคารทำให้หิ่งห้อยน้อยลง ผลที่ว่าต้นไม้ไกลจากอาคารมีหิ่งห้อยมากกว่าต้นไม้ชนิดเดียวกันใกล้อาคารจึงสนับสนุนโดยตรง ถ้าจำนวนเท่ากันจะทำให้สมมติฐานอ่อนลง ส่วนเรื่องเรือท่องเที่ยวและความสูงของต้นไม้ไม่เกี่ยวกับแสงและจำนวนหิ่งห้อย"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"central-ideas","difficulty":"m","passage":"The following text is from a short story.\nArun had practised the piece for months, but on the night of the recital his fingers felt like borrowed things. He played the opening bars too quickly, slowed down, and then lost his place altogether. In the silence, he looked up and saw his teacher in the second row, nodding calmly, as if a pause were simply part of the music. Arun took a breath, found the next note, and continued.","stem":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["A nervous performer recovers from a mistake, helped by his teacher's calm reaction.","A teacher interrupts a recital in order to correct a student's errors.","A student decides to stop playing music after a disappointing recital.","A musician performs a difficult piece perfectly despite feeling nervous."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Arun is nervous, loses his place, sees his teacher's calm nod and then continues: he recovers with his teacher's help. He does not give up, the teacher only nods and never interrupts, and the performance is not perfect because he loses his place.","th":"อรุณตื่นเต้น เล่นผิดจนหลงตำแหน่ง แต่เห็นครูพยักหน้าอย่างสงบจึงตั้งสติและเล่นต่อได้ เขาไม่ได้เลิกเล่นดนตรี ครูไม่ได้ขัดจังหวะการแสดง และการแสดงก็ไม่ได้สมบูรณ์แบบเพราะเขาเล่นผิด"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"h","passage":"An economist studying street-food vendors in Bangkok found that vendors who accept QR-code payments report higher daily sales than vendors who accept only cash. However, the vendors who accept QR codes were also much more likely to be located near office buildings, where customers tend to spend more per meal even when they pay in cash. Therefore, the higher sales reported by vendors who accept QR codes ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["indicate that vendors near office buildings rarely accept cash payments.","may be explained at least partly by where those vendors are located rather than by the payment method itself.","show that office workers prefer to pay for street food in cash.","prove that offering QR-code payments causes customers to spend more on each meal."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The text points out a second difference between the groups: location. Since customers near offices spend more even in cash, location could account for some of the higher sales. 'Prove that QR payments cause' ignores this problem; the text never says office workers prefer cash; and it says nothing about vendors near offices refusing cash.","th":"ข้อความชี้ว่าผู้ค้าที่รับ QR มักอยู่ใกล้อาคารสำนักงานซึ่งลูกค้าจ่ายมากกว่าแม้จ่ายเงินสด ยอดขายที่สูงกว่าจึงอาจเกิดจากทำเลมากกว่าวิธีชำระเงิน การบอกว่า 'พิสูจน์ว่า QR ทำให้ลูกค้าจ่ายมากขึ้น' ละเลยปัญหานี้ ข้อความไม่ได้บอกว่าพนักงานออฟฟิศชอบเงินสด และไม่ได้บอกว่าผู้ค้าใกล้สำนักงานไม่รับเงินสด"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":"m","passage":"Many visitors who travel north from Bangkok stop at the historical park in the town of Sukhothai. The ancient city of ______ was the capital of an early Thai kingdom in the thirteenth century, now attracts thousands of tourists every year.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Sukhothai; which","Sukhothai, which","Sukhothai which","Sukhothai: which"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The clause 'which was the capital … century' adds extra information about Sukhothai and is already closed by a comma after 'century', so it must also be opened by a comma: 'Sukhothai, which'. Leaving out the comma breaks the pair, and a semicolon or a colon cannot separate a subject from the rest of its own sentence.","th":"อนุประโยค which was the capital … century เป็นข้อมูลเสริม และมีจุลภาคปิดท้ายหลัง century แล้ว จึงต้องมีจุลภาคเปิดหน้าด้วย คือ Sukhothai, which การไม่ใส่จุลภาคทำให้ไม่เป็นคู่ ส่วน ; และ : ไม่สามารถใช้แยกประธานออกจากส่วนที่เหลือของประโยคเดียวกันได้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"form-structure-sense","difficulty":"m","passage":"Poison dart frogs of Central and South America are among the most brightly coloured animals on Earth. The vivid colours of the frog's skin ______ predators that the animal is toxic and should not be eaten.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["has warned","warns","warn","is warning"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The subject of the verb is 'colours' (plural), not 'skin' or 'frog', so the plural verb 'warn' is needed. 'Warns', 'has warned' and 'is warning' are all singular forms that would agree only with a singular subject.","th":"ประธานของกริยาคือ colours (พหูพจน์) ไม่ใช่ skin หรือ frog จึงต้องใช้ warn ส่วน warns, has warned และ is warning เป็นรูปเอกพจน์ ใช้กับประธานเอกพจน์เท่านั้น"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"e","passage":"Durian, a fruit grown widely in Thailand and Malaysia, is famous for its powerful smell, which many people find unpleasant. ______ a number of hotels and train services in the region do not allow passengers or guests to bring durian inside.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In contrast,","For instance,","Similarly,","As a result,"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The ban on durian is a consequence of its strong smell, so 'As a result' is the logical transition. 'In contrast' signals an opposing idea, 'Similarly' signals a comparable point, and 'For instance' introduces an example, but the second sentence is an effect of the first.","th":"การห้ามนำทุเรียนเข้าโรงแรมและรถไฟเป็นผลมาจากกลิ่นแรง จึงใช้ As a result ส่วน In contrast ใช้กับความขัดแย้ง Similarly ใช้กับสิ่งที่คล้ายกัน และ For instance ใช้ยกตัวอย่าง ซึ่งไม่ตรงกับความสัมพันธ์แบบเหตุและผล"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"m","passage":"Traditional Thai houses were often built on tall wooden stilts, which kept the living areas above the water during the rainy-season floods. ______ the raised floors allowed cool air to move beneath the house, making the rooms more comfortable during the hot season.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In other words,","Instead,","Nevertheless,","Moreover,"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The second sentence adds a second benefit of building on stilts, so 'Moreover' is correct. 'Nevertheless' signals a contrast, 'Instead' signals a replacement, and 'In other words' signals a restatement, but cooler rooms is a new advantage, not a restatement of flood protection.","th":"ประโยคที่สองเพิ่มข้อดีอีกข้อของบ้านใต้ถุนสูง จึงใช้ Moreover ส่วน Nevertheless แสดงความขัดแย้ง Instead แสดงการแทนที่ และ In other words ใช้กล่าวซ้ำด้วยคำอื่น แต่ความเย็นเป็นข้อดีใหม่ ไม่ใช่การกล่าวซ้ำเรื่องน้ำท่วม"}}]}},{"exam":"sat","set":2,"title":{"en":"SAT Reading and Writing — Practice module 2","th":"SAT Reading and Writing — ชุดฝึก 2"},"note":{"en":"One 27-question module in Digital SAT format. DeepDistrict practice — not an official College Board test.","th":"1 โมดูล 27 ข้อ รูปแบบ Digital SAT — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการของ College Board"},"minutes":32,"kinds":{"sat":27},"subjects":{},"free":false,"file":"sat-2","sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"e","passage":"Before recording technology existed, a folk song survived only if people remembered it and taught it to others. Many songs from rural Isan were ______ in exactly this way, passed from parents to children over many generations until researchers finally wrote them down in the twentieth century.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["preserved","exaggerated","invented","forbidden"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The songs 'survived' because people remembered them and taught them, so they were 'preserved' (kept in existence). 'Invented' would describe how a song begins, not how it survives; 'forbidden' and 'exaggerated' do not fit songs being passed on faithfully.","th":"เพลงอยู่รอดมาได้เพราะคนจดจำและสอนต่อกัน จึงหมายถึง preserved (รักษาไว้) ส่วน invented (คิดค้นขึ้น) พูดถึงการเริ่มต้นของเพลง ไม่ใช่การอยู่รอด forbidden (ถูกห้าม) และ exaggerated (ถูกพูดเกินจริง) ไม่เข้ากับการสืบทอดเพลง"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"m","passage":"Although her first novels sold only a few hundred copies, critics now regard the writer as ______ figure in modern Thai literature: her experiments with shifting narrators shaped the work of an entire generation of younger authors.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["an obscure","a conventional","a reluctant","a pivotal"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"A writer who 'shaped the work of an entire generation' is of central importance, so 'a pivotal' fits. 'An obscure' contradicts the word 'now', which contrasts her current reputation with her poor early sales; 'a reluctant' is not supported; and 'a conventional' conflicts with her 'experiments'.","th":"นักเขียนที่มีอิทธิพลต่อนักเขียนทั้งรุ่นย่อมมีความสำคัญมาก จึงเป็น a pivotal (สำคัญเป็นจุดเปลี่ยน) ส่วน an obscure (ไม่มีใครรู้จัก) ขัดกับคำว่า now ซึ่งแสดงว่าชื่อเสียงปัจจุบันต่างจากยอดขายช่วงแรก a reluctant (ไม่เต็มใจ) ไม่มีข้อมูลสนับสนุน และ a conventional (ตามขนบ) ขัดกับคำว่า experiments"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"h","passage":"Neuroscientist Lalita Boonmee's experiments showed a clear link between deep sleep and memory in mice. In presenting her results, however, Boonmee was careful to ______ her conclusions, noting that the effect had not yet been tested in humans and might not appear in animals with different sleep patterns.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["exaggerate","qualify","repudiate","substantiate"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"'However' and the limits she mentions show that Boonmee restricted her claims, which is what 'qualify' means. 'Substantiate' (support with more evidence) does not match pointing out what has not been tested, 'exaggerate' is the opposite of being careful, and 'repudiate' (reject completely) is too strong, since her mouse results were clear.","th":"คำว่า however และการที่เธอชี้ข้อจำกัด แสดงว่าเธอจำกัดขอบเขตข้อสรุป ซึ่งคือ qualify ส่วน substantiate (ยืนยันด้วยหลักฐาน) ไม่ตรงกับการบอกว่ายังไม่ได้ทดสอบ exaggerate (พูดเกินจริง) ตรงข้ามกับความระมัดระวัง และ repudiate (ปฏิเสธโดยสิ้นเชิง) รุนแรงเกินไปเพราะผลในหนูชัดเจน"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"e","passage":"Seeds of the sacred lotus can remain alive for an extraordinarily long time. In one study, scientists planted lotus seeds that had been buried in a dry lakebed for several centuries, and many of them sprouted and grew into healthy plants. This finding suggests that, under the right conditions, lotus seeds ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["grow best when they are planted in dry soil.","lose their ability to sprout once they are buried.","can remain able to grow for hundreds of years.","must be planted within a year after they form."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"Seeds buried for 'several centuries' still sprouted, so lotus seeds can stay alive and able to grow for hundreds of years. This contradicts the claims that they must be planted within a year and that burial destroys their ability to sprout, and the text says nothing about planting in dry soil.","th":"เมล็ดที่ถูกฝังอยู่หลายร้อยปียังงอกได้ จึงสรุปว่าเมล็ดบัวมีชีวิตอยู่ได้หลายร้อยปี ซึ่งขัดกับข้อที่ว่าต้องปลูกภายในหนึ่งปีหรือการถูกฝังทำให้งอกไม่ได้ และข้อความไม่ได้กล่าวถึงการปลูกในดินแห้ง"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"evidence-textual","difficulty":"m","passage":"Public libraries in Bangkok were once used mainly for borrowing books. A city researcher claims that, in recent years, these libraries have increasingly become places where people come to work and study rather than places to borrow books.","stem":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support the researcher's claim?","choices":["Over the past five years, both the number of visitors and the number of books borrowed have stayed about the same.","Over the past five years, the number of visitors using library desks and Wi-Fi has risen, while the number of books borrowed has fallen.","Most library visitors surveyed said that they enjoy reading novels in their free time.","Over the past five years, libraries have added thousands of new books to their collections."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The claim describes a shift: more people using libraries as workspaces and fewer borrowing books. Rising use of desks and Wi-Fi together with falling loans shows exactly that. Enjoying novels and adding books say nothing about how the libraries are used, and unchanged numbers would suggest no shift at all.","th":"ข้ออ้างพูดถึงการเปลี่ยนแปลง คือคนใช้ห้องสมุดเป็นที่ทำงานมากขึ้นและยืมหนังสือน้อยลง การที่ผู้ใช้โต๊ะและ Wi-Fi เพิ่มขึ้นแต่การยืมหนังสือลดลงจึงสนับสนุนโดยตรง การชอบอ่านนิยายและการเพิ่มหนังสือไม่ได้บอกวิธีใช้ห้องสมุด และตัวเลขที่ไม่เปลี่ยนแปลงแสดงว่าไม่มีการเปลี่ยนแปลงเลย"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"h","passage":"Astronomers observing a distant star noticed that its brightness dips by the same small amount every 12 days. Regular dips like these are often caused by a planet passing in front of a star. A dark spot on the star's surface, rotating in and out of view, can also cause regular dips, but such spots usually grow and shrink over a few weeks, which makes the dips vary in depth. Because the dips have stayed exactly the same depth throughout two years of observation, the astronomers concluded that ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["the star has no dark spots anywhere on its surface.","a passing planet is a more likely cause of the dips than a rotating spot.","a planet could not produce dips that stay the same depth.","the star must rotate exactly once every 12 days."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Spots would make the dips change in depth; the dips have not changed, so a planet is the better explanation. The evidence does not show that the star has no spots at all, only that spots are unlikely to cause these dips. A 12-day rotation would matter only for the spot explanation, which the evidence weakens, and the text implies that a planet can produce dips of constant depth.","th":"จุดมืดบนดาวทำให้ความลึกของการหรี่แสงเปลี่ยนไป แต่ความลึกคงที่ตลอดสองปี จึงสรุปว่าดาวเคราะห์โคจรผ่านน่าจะเป็นสาเหตุมากกว่า หลักฐานไม่ได้แสดงว่าดาวไม่มีจุดมืดเลย การหมุนรอบตัวทุก 12 วันเกี่ยวกับคำอธิบายแบบจุดมืดซึ่งถูกหักล้าง และข้อความบอกเป็นนัยว่าดาวเคราะห์ทำให้หรี่แสงคงที่ได้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":"m","passage":"The Phi Ta Khon ______ held each year in the town of Dan Sai in Loei Province, features performers wearing tall, brightly painted masks made from parts of coconut palms and the woven baskets used for steaming sticky rice.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["festival—","festival","festival,","festival;"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The phrase 'held each year … Loei Province' is extra information about the festival and is closed with a comma after 'Province', so it must be opened with a comma: 'festival,'. Without the comma the pair is broken, a semicolon would cut the subject off from its verb 'features', and a dash cannot be paired with a comma.","th":"วลี held each year … Loei Province เป็นข้อมูลเสริมที่ปิดด้วยจุลภาคหลัง Province จึงต้องเปิดด้วยจุลภาค คือ festival, ถ้าไม่ใส่จะไม่ครบคู่ ; จะแยกประธานออกจากกริยา features และขีดยาว (—) ใช้คู่กับจุลภาคไม่ได้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"form-structure-sense","difficulty":"m","passage":"When archaeologists first reached the limestone cave in 2015, they found blackened ceilings and layers of ash on the floor. Local villagers explained that by then, their families ______ the cave as a shelter during storms for centuries.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["had used","will have used","use","are using"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The using of the cave happened over a long period before another past moment ('by then', 2015), so the past perfect 'had used' is correct. 'Use' and 'are using' are present forms, and 'will have used' refers to the future, none of which fits a period ending in 2015.","th":"การใช้ถ้ำเกิดขึ้นต่อเนื่องก่อนจุดเวลาในอดีต (by then คือปี 2015) จึงใช้ past perfect คือ had used ส่วน use และ are using เป็นปัจจุบัน และ will have used เป็นอนาคต ไม่เข้ากับช่วงเวลาที่จบในปี 2015"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"e","passage":"Elephants are known for their excellent memories, which help them survive in harsh environments. ______ older female elephants can lead their herds to water holes that they have not visited for many years.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For example,","However,","Instead,","In contrast,"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Leading the herd to water holes not visited for years is a specific case of elephants' excellent memory, so 'For example' fits. 'However' and 'In contrast' signal a contrast that is not present, and 'Instead' signals a replacement for something.","th":"การพาโขลงไปแหล่งน้ำที่ไม่ได้ไปมาหลายปีเป็นตัวอย่างของความจำดีเยี่ยม จึงใช้ For example ส่วน However และ In contrast แสดงความขัดแย้งซึ่งไม่มีในข้อความ และ Instead แสดงการแทนที่"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"rhetorical-synthesis","difficulty":"m","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- The khim is a Thai hammered dulcimer.\n- It is played by striking its strings with two flexible bamboo sticks.\n- The instrument came to Thailand from China.\n- The jakhe is a Thai zither whose shape was once modelled on a crocodile.\n- The jakhe is played by plucking its strings with a pick tied to the player's finger.","stem":"The student wants to contrast the ways the two instruments are played. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The jakhe is a Thai zither whose shape was once modelled on a crocodile.","The khim, a Thai hammered dulcimer, came to Thailand from China.","While the khim is played by striking its strings with two bamboo sticks, the jakhe is played by plucking its strings with a pick tied to the player's finger.","The khim and the jakhe are both Thai instruments with strings."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"Only the sentence with 'While' describes how each instrument is played and sets the two methods against each other. The sentence about the khim's origin and the sentence about the jakhe's shape each mention only one instrument and not how it is played, and the sentence about both having strings states a similarity, not a contrast.","th":"มีเพียงประโยคที่ใช้ While ที่บอกวิธีเล่นของเครื่องดนตรีทั้งสองชนิดและเปรียบเทียบความต่าง ประโยคเรื่องที่มาของขิมและรูปร่างของจะเข้พูดถึงเครื่องดนตรีชนิดเดียวและไม่ได้บอกวิธีเล่น ส่วนประโยคที่บอกว่าทั้งสองมีสายเป็นความเหมือน ไม่ใช่ความต่าง"}}]}},{"exam":"sat","set":3,"title":{"en":"SAT Reading and Writing — Practice module 3","th":"SAT Reading and Writing — ชุดฝึก 3"},"note":{"en":"One 27-question module in Digital SAT format. DeepDistrict practice — not an official College Board test.","th":"1 โมดูล 27 ข้อ รูปแบบ Digital SAT — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการของ College Board"},"minutes":32,"kinds":{"sat":27},"subjects":{},"free":false,"file":"sat-3","sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"e","passage":"Muay Thai is often called \"the art of eight limbs\" because, unlike boxers, who strike only with their fists, muay Thai fighters ______ their fists, elbows, knees, and shins to strike an opponent.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["decorate","neglect","employ","conceal"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The 'eight limbs' are the body parts fighters use to strike, so they 'employ' (use) them. 'Conceal' (hide) and 'neglect' (fail to use) contradict the idea of striking with them, and 'decorate' has nothing to do with fighting.","th":"'แปดอวัยวะ' คือส่วนของร่างกายที่นักมวยใช้ในการโจมตี จึงใช้ employ (ใช้) ส่วน conceal (ซ่อน) และ neglect (ละเลย) ขัดกับการใช้โจมตี และ decorate (ตกแต่ง) ไม่เกี่ยวกับการต่อสู้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"m","passage":"Engineers estimated that the new flood barrier could hold back rising water for at least three days. That figure, they stressed, was conservative: in every test so far, the barrier had performed considerably better than the estimate suggested.","stem":"As used in the text, what does the word \"conservative\" most nearly mean?","choices":["old-fashioned","carefully protected","cautiously low","politically traditional"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The barrier performed 'considerably better than the estimate', so the estimate was deliberately low to be safe: 'cautiously low'. 'Politically traditional' and 'old-fashioned' are other senses of the word that do not describe a number, and 'carefully protected' relates to 'conserve' but does not fit an estimate.","th":"แนวกั้นทำงานได้ดีกว่าตัวเลขที่ประมาณไว้มาก แสดงว่าวิศวกรประมาณไว้ต่ำเพื่อความปลอดภัย conservative จึงหมายถึง cautiously low ส่วน politically traditional และ old-fashioned เป็นความหมายอื่นของคำนี้ซึ่งใช้กับตัวเลขไม่ได้ และ carefully protected ใกล้กับคำว่า conserve แต่ไม่เข้ากับการประมาณค่า"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"h","passage":"The following text is from a short story.\nSomchai had always believed that his father disliked the sea. The old man never swam, never fished, and turned his face away whenever the family drove along the coast road. So when Somchai found, in the bottom drawer of his father's desk, a thick stack of hand-drawn charts of the Gulf of Thailand, every reef and sandbar marked in careful ink, he sat down slowly, the pages trembling in his hands.","stem":"Which choice best describes the function of the first two sentences in the text as a whole?","choices":["They explain why Somchai's father kept the charts hidden in his desk.","They establish a belief that the discovery described in the final sentence calls into question.","They describe the room in which Somchai finds the charts.","They suggest that Somchai shares his father's dislike of the sea."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The first two sentences set up Somchai's belief and the evidence for it; the charts, drawn with great care, suggest his father had a deep interest in the sea, which is why Somchai is shaken. The text never gives a reason for hiding the charts, the opening sentences describe the father's habits rather than a room, and nothing indicates Somchai himself dislikes the sea.","th":"สองประโยคแรกวางความเชื่อของสมชายและเหตุผลที่เขาเชื่อ แผนที่ทะเลที่วาดอย่างประณีตในประโยคสุดท้ายทำให้ความเชื่อนั้นสั่นคลอน ข้อความไม่ได้บอกเหตุผลที่พ่อซ่อนแผนที่ สองประโยคแรกบรรยายพฤติกรรมของพ่อ ไม่ใช่ห้อง และไม่มีอะไรบอกว่าสมชายไม่ชอบทะเล"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"central-ideas","difficulty":"m","passage":"The following text is from a poem.\nMy grandmother's hands remember\nwhat her memory has let go:\nthe fold that shapes a banana-leaf cup,\nthe twist that closes a jasmine garland,\nthe exact pinch of salt for the curry\nwhose name she can no longer say.","stem":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["The grandmother has forgotten how to make garlands and banana-leaf cups.","The speaker is learning to cook traditional dishes from her grandmother.","Skills learned through long practice can remain even after other memories have faded.","Folding banana-leaf cups is more difficult than making jasmine garlands."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The grandmother has lost some memories (the curry's name) but her hands still know how to fold, twist and season, so practised skills outlast other memories. The poem never shows the speaker learning to cook, it says the hands do remember how to make the cups and garlands, and it does not compare the difficulty of the tasks.","th":"คุณยายลืมบางอย่าง (ชื่อแกง) แต่มือยังจำวิธีพับกระทง ร้อยมาลัย และปรุงรสได้ ใจความหลักคือทักษะที่ฝึกมานานยังคงอยู่แม้ความทรงจำอื่นจะเลือนไป บทกวีไม่ได้บอกว่าผู้พูดกำลังเรียนทำอาหาร บอกว่ามือยังจำวิธีทำกระทงและมาลัยได้ และไม่ได้เปรียบเทียบความยาก"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"evidence-quantitative","difficulty":"m","passage":"Durian flowers open in the late afternoon and are visited by several kinds of animals during the night. A student researcher recorded the average number of visits that three types of visitors made to a group of durian flowers during three periods. Bats made the most visits overall. However, bats were not the most frequent visitors in every period: ______","table":{"title":"Average visits to durian flowers per night","rows":[["Visitor","Before 8 p.m.","8 p.m. to midnight","After midnight"],["Bats","2","14","9"],["Moths","5","3","1"],["Honeybees","1","0","0"]]},"stem":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?","choices":["after midnight, bats made more visits than moths and honeybees combined.","before 8 p.m., honeybees visited the flowers more often than moths did.","between 8 p.m. and midnight, bats made more visits than in any other period.","before 8 p.m., moths visited the flowers more often than bats did."],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The statement needs a period in which another visitor beat the bats. Before 8 p.m., moths made 5 visits and bats only 2. The figures after midnight (9 for bats against 1 and 0) and between 8 p.m. and midnight (14) are true but show bats leading, and honeybees (1) did not visit more often than moths (5) before 8 p.m.","th":"ต้องหาช่วงเวลาที่มีผู้มาเยือนชนิดอื่นมากกว่าค้างคาว คือก่อน 20.00 น. ผีเสื้อกลางคืนมา 5 ครั้ง ค้างคาวมาเพียง 2 ครั้ง ข้อมูลหลังเที่ยงคืน (ค้างคาว 9 ครั้ง) และช่วง 20.00–24.00 น. (14 ครั้ง) เป็นจริงแต่ค้างคาวยังนำอยู่ และผึ้ง (1 ครั้ง) ไม่ได้มามากกว่าผีเสื้อกลางคืน (5 ครั้ง) ก่อน 20.00 น."}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"h","passage":"A psychologist found that students who studied a list of vocabulary words in the evening and were tested after a night's sleep recalled more words than students who studied in the morning and were tested that evening, the same number of hours later. Some critics suggested that the morning group simply encountered more distracting information during the day. To test this, the psychologist added a third group that studied in the morning and then rested quietly, awake, in a dim room until the test. If this group's recall turns out to be similar to that of the original morning group, it would suggest that ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["studying in the morning generally leads to better recall than studying in the evening.","resting quietly while awake helps memory just as much as sleeping does.","daytime distractions were the main reason the morning group recalled fewer words.","sleep itself, rather than simply avoiding daytime distractions, helped the evening group remember more words."],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The quiet-rest group avoids distractions but does not sleep. If it does no better than the morning group, avoiding distractions did not help, so sleep is the likelier reason for the evening group's advantage. That result would count against distractions as the main cause and against quiet rest being as good as sleep, and the original finding showed the evening group, not the morning group, recalling more.","th":"กลุ่มที่พักเงียบ ๆ ไม่เจอสิ่งรบกวนแต่ไม่ได้นอน ถ้าจำได้ไม่ต่างจากกลุ่มเช้า แสดงว่าการเลี่ยงสิ่งรบกวนไม่ได้ช่วย การนอนหลับจึงน่าจะเป็นเหตุที่กลุ่มเย็นจำได้มากกว่า ผลนี้ขัดกับการบอกว่าสิ่งรบกวนเป็นสาเหตุหลัก ขัดกับการบอกว่าการพักผ่อนช่วยได้เท่าการนอน และผลเดิมแสดงว่ากลุ่มเย็นจำได้มากกว่ากลุ่มเช้า"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"form-structure-sense","difficulty":"m","passage":"The film about a family of fishermen in Trang Province was kept secret until its premiere. Neither the director nor the actors ______ willing to discuss its surprising ending with reporters before the opening night.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["is","were","has been","was"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"With 'neither … nor', the verb agrees with the nearer subject, 'the actors', which is plural, and the story is set in the past, so 'were' is correct. 'Was' and 'has been' are singular, and 'is' is singular and in the present tense.","th":"เมื่อใช้ neither … nor กริยาต้องสอดคล้องกับประธานตัวที่ใกล้กว่า คือ the actors ซึ่งเป็นพหูพจน์ และเหตุการณ์เป็นอดีต จึงใช้ were ส่วน was และ has been เป็นเอกพจน์ และ is เป็นเอกพจน์ปัจจุบัน"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":"h","passage":"After the severe floods of 2011, engineers who studied Bangkok's drainage system reached a sobering ______ the city's canals, many of them narrowed by decades of construction along their banks, could carry only a fraction of the water they had once handled.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["conclusion, which","conclusion, that","conclusion,","conclusion:"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The first part is a complete clause, and what follows states the conclusion itself, so a colon is correct. A comma would create a comma splice between two independent clauses, a comma before 'that' wrongly separates the noun 'conclusion' from the clause that tells what the conclusion was, and 'which' makes the sentence ungrammatical because the clause after it already has its own subject, 'the city's canals'.","th":"ส่วนแรกเป็นประโยคสมบูรณ์ และส่วนหลังบอกเนื้อหาของข้อสรุป จึงใช้ : การใช้จุลภาคเป็น comma splice การใส่จุลภาคหน้า that แยกคำนาม conclusion ออกจากอนุประโยคที่บอกเนื้อหาของข้อสรุปโดยไม่ถูกต้อง และการใช้ which ทำให้ผิดไวยากรณ์เพราะอนุประโยคหลังมีประธานของตัวเองแล้ว (the city's canals)"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"e","passage":"Bamboo is a type of grass, not a tree, and it is one of the fastest-growing plants on Earth. ______ some species can grow nearly a metre in a single day under ideal conditions.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Instead,","Otherwise,","In fact,","However,"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The second sentence gives a striking detail that strengthens the claim that bamboo grows very fast, so 'In fact' fits. 'However' would signal a contrast, 'Instead' a replacement, and 'Otherwise' an alternative outcome, none of which matches a supporting detail.","th":"ประโยคที่สองให้รายละเอียดที่ย้ำว่าไผ่โตเร็วมาก จึงใช้ In fact ส่วน However แสดงความขัดแย้ง Instead แสดงการแทนที่ และ Otherwise แสดงผลที่ต่างออกไป ซึ่งไม่ตรงกับการเสริมข้อมูล"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"h","passage":"For years, the coral reef around a small island in the Gulf of Thailand had been in decline. After fishing near the reef was banned in 2010, the number of fish there began to rise steadily. ______ coral cover continued to fall until 2016, when divers began removing the coral-eating starfish that had multiplied on the reef; only after that did the coral start to recover.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Likewise,","As a result,","For instance,","Even so,"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The fishing ban helped the fish, but the coral kept declining anyway, so the third sentence contrasts with what came before: 'Even so'. 'As a result' would make the falling coral a result of more fish, 'For instance' would treat it as an example of fish numbers rising, and 'Likewise' would suggest the coral improved in the same way.","th":"การห้ามประมงทำให้ปลาเพิ่มขึ้น แต่ปะการังยังคงลดลง ประโยคที่สามจึงขัดแย้งกับสิ่งที่กล่าวมาก่อน ต้องใช้ Even so ส่วน As a result ทำให้ปะการังลดลงดูเป็นผลจากปลาเพิ่มขึ้น For instance ทำให้ดูเป็นตัวอย่างของการที่ปลาเพิ่มขึ้น และ Likewise ทำให้ดูเหมือนปะการังดีขึ้นเช่นกัน"}}]}},{"exam":"ielts","set":1,"title":{"en":"IELTS Academic — Practice test 1 (Reading + Writing)","th":"IELTS Academic — ชุดฝึก 1 (Reading + Writing)"},"note":{"en":"Reading: 3 passages, 40 questions, 60 minutes. Writing: Task 1 + Task 2, 60 minutes. DeepDistrict practice — not an official IELTS test.","th":"Reading 3 บทความ 40 ข้อ 60 นาที · Writing Task 1 + Task 2 60 นาที — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการ"},"minutes":60,"kinds":{"ielts-r":3,"ielts-w":2},"subjects":{},"free":true,"file":"ielts-1","sample":{"reading":[{"kind":"ielts-r","title":"Archives in the ice","topic":{"en":"Climate science and glaciology","th":"วิทยาศาสตร์ภูมิอากาศและธารน้ำแข็ง"},"difficulty":1,"labelled":true,"paragraphs":["The ice sheets of Antarctica and Greenland are the most detailed archives of the Earth's past climate that scientists possess. Each year's snowfall is buried by the next, and over millennia the accumulated layers are compressed into ice that may be more than three kilometres thick. Locked inside are traces of the atmosphere and dust of the time when the snow fell. The longest continuous record recovered so far reaches back roughly 800,000 years, and several international teams are now drilling in the hope of extending it to well over a million.","Snow does not become ice overnight. Freshly fallen snow is mostly air. As it is buried, the crystals are rounded and packed more tightly into a granular material known as firn, through which air can still move between the grains. Only at a depth of somewhere between 50 and 100 metres do the pores finally close, sealing small samples of air into bubbles. One consequence is easily overlooked: because air continues to circulate through the firn for decades or centuries after the snow itself has fallen, the gas in any bubble is younger than the ice that surrounds it. At sites where little snow accumulates, the difference can amount to several thousand years, and it must be calculated with care before the records of gas and of ice can be compared.","Drilling teams generally select a dome or a ridge on the ice sheet, where there is minimal horizontal flow, so that the layers lie undisturbed in the order in which they were laid down. A hollow drill extracts a cylinder of ice, which is raised in sections of around three metres and stored at minus 20 degrees Celsius or colder. A particular difficulty arises at intermediate depths, typically between about 600 and 1,200 metres. Here the bubbles are under great pressure, and when the ice is brought up and the confining weight above it is removed, it tends to crack and even shatter. Ice from this so-called brittle zone is therefore commonly left to rest in a storage trench beneath the surface, sometimes for a whole year, while the pressure slowly equalises before it is cut.","Establishing the age of each layer is the next challenge. In the upper part of a core, annual layers can be counted much like tree rings, using visible bands as well as chemical signals that peak in a particular season. Deeper down, however, the weight of the overlying ice stretches the layers so thin that they can no longer be distinguished, and researchers turn instead to computer models of how the ice has flowed. These models are anchored by fixed points such as layers of volcanic ash or sulphate from eruptions whose dates are known independently. Very large eruptions deposit material in both hemispheres, which allows cores from Greenland and Antarctica to be placed on a common timescale.","Past temperatures can be read from the water itself. Molecules containing heavier isotopes of oxygen and hydrogen condense more readily than lighter ones, so the colder the air, the smaller the share of heavy molecules that reaches the polar snow. By measuring this ratio, scientists can estimate the temperature at which the snow formed. The method has pitfalls. The relationship between the ratio and temperature is usually calibrated using differences between places today, and there is no guarantee that it held in the past. If, for instance, a greater proportion of the year's snow fell in summer during some earlier period, the record would suggest a warmer climate than actually existed. An independent check comes from the borehole itself: the ice retains a faint memory of past surface temperatures, which can be measured with sensitive thermometers lowered down the hole. In central Greenland, such measurements indicated that the coldest part of the last glacial period had been substantially colder than the isotopes alone had implied.","Greenhouse gases are measured as well. When samples are crushed in a vacuum, the air released from the bubbles can be analysed directly. Over the past 800,000 years, the concentration of carbon dioxide rose and fell between roughly 180 parts per million in glacial periods and about 280 in warm intervals; today it exceeds 420. Antarctic ice is preferred for these measurements. Greenland ice contains more dust and other impurities, and chemical reactions between them can generate additional carbon dioxide inside the ice, distorting the record, although Greenland cores remain invaluable for methane and for precise dating.","The search is now on for ice that is 1.5 million years old or more. Such a record would cover a puzzling period about a million years ago when the rhythm of ice ages changed from cycles of roughly 41,000 years to cycles of around 100,000 years. At the base of the thickest ice sheets, heat escaping from the rock below can melt the oldest layers away. Candidate sites are identified through airborne radar surveys that reveal the internal structure of the ice and the temperature conditions at its base. Even where ancient ice survives, the deepest layers are so compressed that a single metre may contain more than 10,000 years."],"groups":[{"type":"tfng","instructions":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","questions":[{"text":"The air sealed into a layer of ice is of the same age as the frozen snow that encloses it.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Sections of core from intermediate depths are usually cut up as soon as they reach the surface.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Volcanic material is found more frequently in Greenland cores than in Antarctic ones.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]},{"text":"A change in the season when most snow falls could make a past climate appear warmer than it was.","answer":["TRUE"]},{"text":"Temperature measurements made in a borehole suggested that the last ice age had been less severe than isotope evidence indicated.","answer":["FALSE"]}]},{"type":"matching-info","instructions":"Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–G. NB You may use any letter more than once.","questions":[{"text":"a way of testing an estimate by using a separate source of evidence","answer":["E"]},{"text":"a means of matching records taken from opposite ends of the globe","answer":["D"]},{"text":"the reason why some ice is not processed immediately after it is drilled","answer":["C"]},{"text":"an assumption about the present that may not apply to the distant past","answer":["E"]}]},{"type":"flowchart-completion","instructions":"Complete the flow-chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.","wordLimit":{"words":2,"number":false},"context":"From snowfall to dated sample\n\nFresh snow is buried by later snowfall\n↓\nGrains become rounder and are packed into (10) ______, through which air can still circulate\n↓\nAt 50–100 metres the pores close and air is trapped in (11) ______\n↓\nDrilling takes place on a dome or ridge where there is little (12) ______, so the layers stay in order\n↓\nIn the upper core, (13) ______ are counted; deeper down, flow models are fixed to dated eruptions","questions":[{"text":"(10) ______","answer":["firn"]},{"text":"(11) ______","answer":["bubbles"]},{"text":"(12) ______","answer":["horizontal flow"]},{"text":"(13) ______","answer":["annual layers"]}]}]}],"writing":[{"kind":"ielts-w","task":1,"visual":"table","prompt":"The table below shows the average number of hours per week that boys and girls aged 13–17 in one country spent on five activities outside school hours in 2010 and 2025.\n\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\nWrite at least 150 words.","table":{"title":"Average hours per week spent on activities outside school, ages 13–17","rows":[["Activity","Boys 2010","Girls 2010","Boys 2025","Girls 2025"],["Social media and messaging","4.5","6.0","13.0","17.5"],["Homework and private study","7.0","8.5","6.5","8.0"],["Sport and exercise","6.5","4.0","4.5","3.0"],["Reading for pleasure","3.0","4.5","1.5","2.5"],["Paid part-time work","2.5","2.0","1.0","1.5"]]}},{"kind":"ielts-w","task":2,"essayType":"opinion","prompt":"Now that artificial intelligence tools can produce fluent essays in seconds, some educators argue that schools should stop setting written homework altogether and assess students' writing only under supervision in the classroom.\n\nTo what extent do you agree or disagree?\n\nGive reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.\n\nWrite at least 250 words."}]}},{"exam":"ielts","set":2,"title":{"en":"IELTS Academic — Practice test 2 (Reading + Writing)","th":"IELTS Academic — ชุดฝึก 2 (Reading + Writing)"},"note":{"en":"Reading: 3 passages, 40 questions, 60 minutes. Writing: Task 1 + Task 2, 60 minutes. DeepDistrict practice — not an official IELTS test.","th":"Reading 3 บทความ 40 ข้อ 60 นาที · Writing Task 1 + Task 2 60 นาที — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการ"},"minutes":60,"kinds":{"ielts-r":3,"ielts-w":2},"subjects":{},"free":false,"file":"ielts-2","sample":{"reading":[{"kind":"ielts-r","title":"Frozen assets: the rise and fall of the ice trade","difficulty":2,"topic":{"en":"Economic history","th":"ประวัติศาสตร์เศรษฐกิจ"},"paragraphs":["Before the age of electricity, keeping anything cold in a hot climate was a luxury reserved for the very wealthy. Rulers in Persia, China and the Mediterranean had stored winter snow in pits and thick-walled buildings for centuries, but the quantities were small and the cold rarely travelled far. That changed in the nineteenth century, when an unlikely industry grew up around a resource that seemed, to most people, entirely worthless: the ice that formed each winter on the lakes and ponds of New England. Within a few decades, frozen water cut from those ponds was being sold in the Caribbean, in South America and as far away as India.","The industry is usually traced to Frederic Tudor, a young Boston merchant who in 1806 sent a ship loaded with ice to the Caribbean island of Martinique. His contemporaries thought the plan absurd, and the first voyages appeared to prove them right. Much of the cargo melted before it could be sold, and the islanders who received the rest had little idea what to do with it. Tudor's difficulty, however, was not the crossing itself; ice packed tightly in a ship's hold melts far more slowly than most people expected. The real problem lay at the destination, where there was nowhere to keep the ice once it had been unloaded. Only after years of heavy losses, including a spell in prison for debt, did he begin to build insulated ice houses in the ports he supplied.","Two developments turned this fragile business into a profitable one. The first was the choice of insulation. Early shippers had experimented with straw, hay and rice husks, but sawdust proved the most effective, and it had the additional merit of being almost free, since the timber mills of Maine produced it in enormous quantities as waste. The second was the mechanisation of harvesting. Cutting ice by hand with axes and saws produced blocks of uneven size that wasted space in storage and in transit. A horse-drawn cutter, introduced by one of Tudor's suppliers, Nathaniel Wyeth, scored the frozen surface of a pond in a regular grid, so that workers could split it into identical blocks that could be stacked with almost no gaps between them. Tightly stacked blocks melted more slowly, because less of their surface was exposed to warm air.","With these improvements, the trade expanded rapidly. In 1833 a cargo of ice left Boston for Calcutta, a voyage of around four months that took the ship twice across the equator; more than half of the ice was still frozen when it arrived. By the middle of the century, ships were carrying ice to ports throughout the tropics, and the ponds around Boston had become so valuable that the rights to harvest them were bought and sold like farmland. The writer Henry David Thoreau, who lived for two years beside Walden Pond, recorded watching a large team of labourers remove ice from its surface one winter, and reflected that the water he drank might one day cool a glass in India.","Yet the largest market for natural ice was never overseas. As cities in the United States grew, so did the demand for ice at home. Households bought it to fill wooden iceboxes, in which food could be kept fresh for several days, while brewers needed it to produce lager, a style of beer that must be fermented at low temperatures. Meat-packers in the Midwest packed ice into railway wagons to send fresh beef to the cities of the east coast, an innovation that changed the national diet. In Europe a similar pattern emerged, although most of the supply came not from America but from Norway, whose lakes provided ice that was shipped across the North Sea to British ports in huge quantities.","The success of the industry concealed two weaknesses. The first was its dependence on the weather. A mild winter could leave the ponds too thin to cut, and in such years the price of ice rose sharply; the shortages that followed were known as ice famines. The second weakness was purity. As towns grew along rivers and lakes, the water that froze into ice was increasingly polluted by sewage and industrial waste, and doctors began to warn that the same ice that preserved food could also spread disease. Public confidence, once lost, proved hard to restore.","These problems created an opening for a competitor. Machines that produced ice by compressing and expanding gases had existed since the middle of the century, but they had been expensive and unreliable. As the technology improved, factory-made ice, known in the trade as plant ice, became cheaper; made from filtered water, it could be produced in any season and in any town, close to the customers who needed it. The arrival of affordable electric refrigerators in private homes during the 1920s and 1930s removed the need for regular ice deliveries, and an industry that had once employed tens of thousands of people faded almost entirely from public memory."],"groups":[{"type":"tfng","instructions":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.\n\nQuestions 1–5","questions":[{"text":"Tudor's early ventures failed chiefly because the ice melted quickly during the sea voyage.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"One reason for using sawdust as insulation was its low cost.","answer":["TRUE"]},{"text":"Blocks of ice cut by hand were generally heavier than those cut with Wyeth's equipment.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]},{"text":"European demand for ice was met largely by imports from the United States.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Warnings from doctors led to a ban on selling ice taken from polluted rivers.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]}]},{"type":"matching-info","instructions":"Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–G.\n\nQuestions 6–8","questions":[{"text":"a contrast between the assumed cause of a commercial failure and its actual cause","answer":["B"]},{"text":"a reference to methods of preserving cold that existed long before the ice trade","answer":["A"]},{"text":"an explanation of why a rival product was more convenient for buyers","answer":["G"]}]},{"type":"note-completion","instructions":"Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.\n\nQuestions 9–11","wordLimit":{"words":1,"number":false},"context":"Uses of natural ice within the United States\n• Households: kept food fresh in (9) ______\n• Brewers: needed low temperatures to make (10) ______\n• Meat-packers: sent beef east in railway (11) ______","questions":[{"text":"(9) ______","answer":["iceboxes"]},{"text":"(10) ______","answer":["lager"]},{"text":"(11) ______","answer":["wagons"]}]},{"type":"short-answer","instructions":"Answer the questions below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage for each answer.\n\nQuestions 12–13","wordLimit":{"words":2,"number":false},"questions":[{"text":"What name was given to the shortages that followed unusually warm winters?","answer":["ice famines"]},{"text":"What term did the industry use for ice manufactured by machines?","answer":["plant ice"]}]}]}],"writing":[{"kind":"ielts-w","task":1,"visual":"table","prompt":"The table below gives information about public transport in five cities in 2024.\n\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\nWrite at least 150 words.","table":{"title":"Public transport in five cities, 2024","rows":[["City","Population (millions)","Rail/metro network (km)","Public transport trips per day (millions)","Commuters using public transport (%)","Single fare (US$)"],["Halvern","8.4","410","9.8","63","1.80"],["Marlow Bay","6.9","40","1.7","21","0.60"],["Corrin","5.2","95","2.9","38","0.90"],["Tessaly","3.6","210","3.1","55","2.60"],["Velden","1.8","0","0.9","34","1.20"]]}},{"kind":"ielts-w","task":2,"essayType":"two-part","prompt":"In many countries, people are living longer than ever before, yet a growing share of those extra years is spent in poor health.\n\nWhy is this happening? What can individuals and governments do to make sure that longer lives are also healthier ones?\n\nGive reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.\n\nWrite at least 250 words."}]}},{"exam":"ielts","set":3,"title":{"en":"IELTS Academic — Practice test 3 (Reading + Writing)","th":"IELTS Academic — ชุดฝึก 3 (Reading + Writing)"},"note":{"en":"Reading: 3 passages, 40 questions, 60 minutes. Writing: Task 1 + Task 2, 60 minutes. DeepDistrict practice — not an official IELTS test.","th":"Reading 3 บทความ 40 ข้อ 60 นาที · Writing Task 1 + Task 2 60 นาที — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบทางการ"},"minutes":60,"kinds":{"ielts-r":3,"ielts-w":2},"subjects":{},"free":false,"file":"ielts-3","sample":{"reading":[{"kind":"ielts-r","title":"Lessons from Roman concrete","difficulty":2,"labelled":true,"topic":{"en":"Materials science and engineering","th":"วัสดุศาสตร์และวิศวกรรม"},"paragraphs":["Concrete is the most widely used manufactured material on Earth; after water, it is often said to be the substance that people consume in the greatest quantity. Its essential ingredient, cement, is made by heating limestone and clay to around 1,450°C in a kiln, a process that releases carbon dioxide both from the fuel that is burnt and from the limestone itself as it breaks down. Cement manufacture is estimated to account for roughly 8 per cent of global carbon dioxide emissions. Modern reinforced concrete is also surprisingly short-lived: many bridges and buildings from the twentieth century required major repairs within fifty to a hundred years. It is a striking irony, then, that some structures built by the Romans two thousand years ago are still standing, and that a few appear to be stronger now than when they were completed.","Roman builders did not use Portland cement, which was patented in England only in 1824. Instead, they combined lime, produced by heating limestone at lower temperatures than modern kilns reach, with volcanic ash, the finest of which came from deposits around the Bay of Naples. The ash, rich in silica and alumina, reacted with the lime and water to form a binding paste. Writers of the period describe how this mixture was packed down together with chunks of rock or broken brick, rather than poured as a liquid in the way that modern concrete is. The result was denser than might be expected, and its chemistry differed fundamentally from that of the modern material.","The most remarkable examples are the harbour walls and piers that Roman engineers built directly in the sea. For modern concrete, seawater is an enemy: salt penetrates the material and corrodes the steel bars inside, and as the steel rusts and swells, the surrounding concrete cracks. Roman marine concrete contains no steel, and analysis of cores drilled from ancient harbours has revealed something more surprising still. As seawater seeped through the structures over centuries, it dissolved part of the volcanic material and allowed rare minerals to crystallise in the gaps, among them a plate-shaped mineral called aluminous tobermorite. These interlocking crystals appear to have reinforced the material from within, so that contact with the sea, rather than weakening it, gradually made it more cohesive.","A second puzzle concerned the small white lumps of lime scattered through many samples of Roman concrete. Researchers had long dismissed these 'lime clasts' as signs of careless mixing or poor raw materials. More recent studies have proposed another explanation: that the Romans mixed their concrete 'hot', adding quicklime directly instead of first combining it with water. The intense heat of this reaction would have left behind lumps of brittle, calcium-rich material. When a crack later formed and water entered it, the lumps could dissolve and recrystallise as calcium carbonate, sealing the crack. To test the idea, one team made new samples using the hot-mixing method, cracked them deliberately and ran water through them. Within about two weeks the cracks had closed, whereas in otherwise identical samples made without quicklime the water continued to flow.","It would be wrong, however, to conclude that Roman concrete is simply superior. It is considerably weaker in compression than its modern equivalent and takes far longer to reach its full strength, which would be unacceptable on a modern building site, where the timber or metal moulds must be removed and work on the next floor begun within days. Nor could it be used for the slender beams and tall towers of contemporary architecture, which depend on the steel reinforcement that Roman builders did without. Moreover, suitable volcanic ash occurs only in certain regions, and supplying it in the quantities that today's construction industry consumes would be impractical.","What engineers hope to borrow, therefore, is not the Roman recipe but some of its principles. One line of research adds volcanic ash or industrial by-products such as fly ash from power stations to modern mixes, reducing the amount of cement required and, with it, carbon emissions. Another seeks to reproduce the self-healing effect by other means. Some experimental concretes contain dormant bacteria, packed with a food source in tiny capsules; when a crack lets in water, the bacteria become active and produce limestone that fills the gap. Others contain capsules of a liquid healing agent that burst open when the concrete around them cracks.","Whether such materials are adopted widely will depend less on chemistry than on economics and regulation. Self-healing concretes currently cost considerably more than conventional mixes, and building codes, which are based on decades of experience with Portland cement, are slow to accept materials whose long-term behaviour is unknown. Supporters argue that the higher initial price should be weighed against the cost of repairs over a structure's whole life, which can exceed the cost of building it in the first place. If they are right, the most valuable lesson of Roman concrete may be one of perspective: a material should be judged not only by how quickly it can be built with, but by how long it lasts."],"groups":[{"type":"matching-info","instructions":"Reading Passage 1 has seven paragraphs, A–G. Which paragraph contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A–G.","questions":[{"text":"the date when the modern type of cement was first given legal protection","answer":["B"]},{"text":"a feature of the material that was once taken as evidence of poor workmanship","answer":["D"]},{"text":"a reason why the ancient material would delay modern construction projects","answer":["E"]}]},{"type":"tfng","instructions":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","questions":[{"text":"The carbon dioxide released in making cement comes only from the fuel burnt in the kilns.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Roman writers recorded the exact proportions of lime and ash used in their concrete.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]},{"text":"In Roman harbour structures, new minerals formed as a result of seawater passing through the concrete.","answer":["TRUE"]},{"text":"The hot-mixing experiment was carried out on samples taken from ancient buildings.","answer":["FALSE"]},{"text":"Concrete containing capsules of healing agent was developed after concrete containing bacteria.","answer":["NOT GIVEN"]}]},{"type":"table-completion","instructions":"Complete the table below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer.","wordLimit":{"words":1,"number":false},"context":"Roman and modern concrete compared\nFeature | Roman concrete | Modern concrete\nBinder | lime combined with volcanic (9) ______ | Portland cement\nHow it is placed | packed down with chunks of rock or brick | poured as a liquid\nEffect of seawater | crystals strengthen it from within | salt attacks the steel (10) ______ inside\nMain drawbacks | slow to reach full strength; weaker in (11) ______ | short-lived; high carbon emissions","questions":[{"text":"(9) ______","answer":["ash"]},{"text":"(10) ______","answer":["bars"]},{"text":"(11) ______","answer":["compression"]}]},{"type":"mcq-multi","instructions":"Choose TWO letters, A–E.","questions":[{"text":"Which TWO ways of improving modern concrete are being investigated, according to the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"replacing part of the cement with volcanic ash or industrial waste"},{"key":"B","text":"removing steel reinforcement from tall buildings"},{"key":"C","text":"heating limestone to higher temperatures in the kiln"},{"key":"D","text":"importing volcanic ash from the Bay of Naples"},{"key":"E","text":"adding inactive bacteria that produce limestone when water gets in"}],"answer":["A","E"]}]}]}],"writing":[{"kind":"ielts-w","task":1,"visual":"table","prompt":"The table below gives information about the use of public libraries in one country in 2005, 2015 and 2025.\n\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\nWrite at least 150 words.","table":{"title":"Public libraries in one country, 2005–2025","rows":[["","2005","2015","2025"],["Number of libraries","4,620","4,130","3,580"],["Visits (millions)","312","268","241"],["Printed books borrowed (millions)","405","290","176"],["E-books and audiobooks borrowed (millions)","0.4","38","121"],["Average opening hours per week","46","41","43"],["Events held (thousands)","58","84","131"]]}},{"kind":"ielts-w","task":2,"essayType":"discussion","prompt":"Some people argue that governments should fund scientific research only when it is likely to produce practical benefits, such as new medicines or technologies. Others believe that research driven purely by curiosity deserves equal public support, even if it has no obvious use.\n\nDiscuss both these views and give your own opinion.\n\nGive reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.\n\nWrite at least 250 words."}]}},{"exam":"gate","set":1,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 GATE Program — Practice set 1","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 GATE Program — ชุดฝึก 1"},"note":{"en":"40 questions: Mathematics 15, Science 15, English 5, Thai 5. DeepDistrict practice format based on the school's published subjects — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ: คณิตศาสตร์ 15 วิทยาศาสตร์ 15 ภาษาอังกฤษ 5 ภาษาไทย 5 — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ตามวิชาที่โรงเรียนประกาศ ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"subjects":{"math":15,"sci":15,"eng":5,"thai":5},"free":true,"file":"gate-1","sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ห.ร.ม. ของ 84 และ 126 เท่ากับเท่าใด","choices":["252","42","14","21"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"84 = 2²×3×7 and 126 = 2×3²×7. The HCF takes the common primes with the smaller powers: 2×3×7 = 42. (252 is the LCM, not the HCF.)","th":"84 = 2²×3×7 และ 126 = 2×3²×7 ห.ร.ม. คือผลคูณของตัวประกอบเฉพาะที่ซ้ำกันโดยใช้เลขชี้กำลังน้อยกว่า = 2×3×7 = 42 (252 คือ ค.ร.น. ไม่ใช่ ห.ร.ม.)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"รถยนต์คันหนึ่งขับจากเมือง ก ไปเมือง ข ด้วยอัตราเร็ว 60 กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง และขับกลับทางเดิมด้วยอัตราเร็ว 40 กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง อัตราเร็วเฉลี่ยตลอดการเดินทางไป–กลับเป็นกี่กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง","choices":["48","45","52","50"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Average speed = total distance ÷ total time, not the mean of the speeds. Take the distance as 120 km: time = 2 h + 3 h = 5 h, total 240 km, so 240 ÷ 5 = 48 km/h.","th":"อัตราเร็วเฉลี่ย = ระยะทางทั้งหมด ÷ เวลาทั้งหมด ไม่ใช่ค่าเฉลี่ยของอัตราเร็ว สมมติระยะทาง 120 กม. ไปใช้ 2 ชม. กลับใช้ 3 ชม. รวม 240 กม. ใน 5 ชม. ได้ 240 ÷ 5 = 48 กม./ชม."}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"รูปสี่เหลี่ยมจัตุรัสยาวด้านละ 14 เซนติเมตร ที่มุมทั้งสี่วาดส่วนของวงกลม (เสี้ยววงกลม 1/4) รัศมี 7 เซนติเมตร โดยมีจุดศูนย์กลางที่มุมแต่ละมุม พื้นที่ส่วนของจัตุรัสที่ไม่อยู่ในเสี้ยววงกลมใด ๆ เป็นกี่ตารางเซนติเมตร (ใช้ π ≈ 22/7)","choices":["56","42","49","154"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Four quarter circles of radius 7 make one full circle: 22/7 × 7 × 7 = 154 cm². The square is 14 × 14 = 196 cm². Uncovered area = 196 − 154 = 42 cm².","th":"เสี้ยววงกลม 4 ชิ้นรัศมี 7 รวมกันเป็นวงกลม 1 วง พื้นที่ 22/7 × 7 × 7 = 154 ตร.ซม. จัตุรัสมีพื้นที่ 14 × 14 = 196 ตร.ซม. ส่วนที่เหลือ = 196 − 154 = 42 ตร.ซม."}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"โครงสร้างใดพบในเซลล์พืช แต่ไม่พบในเซลล์สัตว์","choices":["เยื่อหุ้มเซลล์","นิวเคลียส","ไมโทคอนเดรีย","ผนังเซลล์"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Plant cells have a cell wall (and chloroplasts) that animal cells lack. Both cell types have a cell membrane, a nucleus and mitochondria.","th":"เซลล์พืชมีผนังเซลล์ (และคลอโรพลาสต์) ซึ่งเซลล์สัตว์ไม่มี ส่วนเยื่อหุ้มเซลล์ นิวเคลียส และไมโทคอนเดรียพบได้ในเซลล์ทั้งสองชนิด"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"วงจรไฟฟ้ามีถ่านไฟฉาย 1 ชุด หลอดไฟ A ต่ออนุกรมกับหลอดไฟ B และ C ซึ่งต่อขนานกันอยู่ (หลอดทั้งสามเหมือนกันทุกประการ) ถ้าคลายหลอด B ออก ความสว่างของหลอด A และ C จะเปลี่ยนไปอย่างไร","choices":["A ไม่เปลี่ยน แต่ C สว่างขึ้น","A สว่างขึ้น และ C สว่างขึ้น","A หรี่ลง และ C หรี่ลง","A หรี่ลง แต่ C สว่างขึ้น"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Before: the circuit resistance is R + R/2 = 1.5R, so bulb A carries V/1.5R and C carries half of that, V/3R. After removing B: resistance = 2R, so A and C both carry V/2R. A's current falls (dimmer) and C's current rises (brighter).","th":"ก่อนคลาย: ความต้านทานรวม R + R/2 = 1.5R กระแสผ่าน A = V/1.5R และผ่าน C ครึ่งหนึ่ง = V/3R หลังคลาย B: ความต้านทานรวม 2R กระแสผ่าน A และ C = V/2R กระแสใน A ลดลงจึงหรี่ลง ส่วนกระแสใน C เพิ่มขึ้นจึงสว่างขึ้น"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":{"title":"ความสูงของต้นถั่วเขียวหลัง 2 สัปดาห์","rows":[["แสงต่อวัน (ชั่วโมง)","0","4","8","12"],["ความสูง (ซม.)","2","6","11","15"]]},"stem":"นักเรียนปลูกต้นถั่วเขียวในกระถาง 4 กระถาง ใช้ดิน น้ำ และพันธุ์เดียวกัน แต่ให้ได้รับแสงต่อวันต่างกัน แล้ววัดความสูงหลัง 2 สัปดาห์ ได้ผลดังตาราง ข้อสรุปใดเหมาะสมที่สุด","choices":["ในช่วงที่ทดลอง ยิ่งได้รับแสงต่อวันนานขึ้น ต้นถั่วเขียวยิ่งสูงมากขึ้น","ถ้าให้แสงวันละ 16 ชั่วโมง ต้นถั่วเขียวจะสูง 19 เซนติเมตรอย่างแน่นอน","ระยะเวลาที่ได้รับแสงเป็นตัวแปรควบคุมของการทดลองนี้","ปริมาณน้ำที่รดเป็นตัวแปรต้นของการทดลองนี้"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Light time is the independent variable (changed on purpose); water, soil and seed type are controlled. Height rises as light time rises from 0 to 12 hours, so that is the supported conclusion. Predicting an exact value at 16 hours goes beyond the data.","th":"ระยะเวลาที่ได้รับแสงเป็นตัวแปรต้น ส่วนน้ำ ดิน และพันธุ์เป็นตัวแปรควบคุม ข้อมูลแสดงว่าเมื่อแสงเพิ่มจาก 0 ถึง 12 ชั่วโมง ความสูงเพิ่มขึ้น จึงสรุปได้ว่ายิ่งได้แสงนานขึ้นยิ่งสูงมากขึ้นในช่วงที่ทดลอง การทำนายค่าแน่นอนที่ 16 ชั่วโมงเกินกว่าข้อมูลที่มี"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct word: My brother ___ to school by bus every day.","choices":["goes","go","gone","going"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"\"Every day\" shows a habit, so we use the present simple. With a singular subject (my brother) the verb takes -es: goes.","th":"\"every day\" บอกกิจวัตร จึงใช้ present simple ประธานเอกพจน์ (my brother) กริยาต้องเติม -es เป็น goes"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the best word: Dr. Suda is very ___. She checks every result three times before she writes her report.","choices":["careless","careful","lazy","noisy"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Checking every result three times shows she pays close attention, so \"careful\" fits. \"Careless\" means the opposite.","th":"การตรวจผลทุกครั้งถึงสามรอบแสดงว่าเธอละเอียดรอบคอบ จึงใช้ careful ส่วน careless มีความหมายตรงข้าม"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"h","passage":"Mangroves grow where rivers meet the sea. Their tangled roots slow down the waves, so the soil behind them is not washed away. Small fish and crabs hide among the roots while they are young, and many of them later move out to the open sea. In the past, large areas of mangroves in Thailand were cut down to make shrimp farms. Today, some villages plant young mangrove trees every year, because they have learned that fewer mangroves mean fewer fish to catch.","table":null,"stem":"What can we infer about many of the fish that the villagers catch in the sea?","choices":["They eat the leaves of mangrove trees.","They can only live where rivers meet the sea.","They spent their early life among mangrove roots.","They are raised in shrimp farms."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The text says young fish hide among the roots and later move to the open sea, and that fewer mangroves mean fewer fish to catch. So many fish caught at sea grew up among the mangrove roots.","th":"บทความบอกว่าปลาตัวเล็กหลบซ่อนอยู่ตามรากโกงกาง แล้วจึงออกไปสู่ทะเลเปิด และป่าชายเลนที่ลดลงทำให้จับปลาได้น้อยลง จึงอนุมานได้ว่าปลาที่จับได้ในทะเลจำนวนมากเคยเติบโตอยู่ตามรากโกงกาง"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"คำราชาศัพท์ที่ใช้แทนคำว่า \"กิน\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์คือคำใด","choices":["เสวย","ประทับ","ทรงพระดำเนิน","บรรทม"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"For the king, \"to eat\" is เสวย. บรรทม means to sleep, ประทับ means to sit or stay, and ทรงพระดำเนิน means to walk.","th":"คำว่า \"กิน\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์ใช้ว่า เสวย ส่วนบรรทม แปลว่า นอน ประทับ แปลว่า นั่งหรืออยู่ และทรงพระดำเนิน แปลว่า เดิน"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ในประโยค \"น้องวิ่งเร็วมาก\" คำว่า \"เร็ว\" เป็นคำชนิดใด","choices":["คำกริยา","คำบุพบท","คำนาม","คำวิเศษณ์"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"เร็ว (fast) describes how the verb วิ่ง (run) is done, so it is an adverb-type word, คำวิเศษณ์. The verb in the sentence is วิ่ง.","th":"\"เร็ว\" ขยายคำกริยา \"วิ่ง\" ว่าวิ่งอย่างไร จึงเป็นคำวิเศษณ์ ส่วนคำกริยาในประโยคคือ \"วิ่ง\""}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"h","passage":"ในอดีต ชาวบ้านริมแม่น้ำเจ้าพระยาใช้เรือเป็นพาหนะหลัก บ้านเรือนจึงหันหน้าเข้าหาแม่น้ำ ตลาดสำคัญก็ตั้งอยู่ริมน้ำ เมื่อมีการตัดถนนมากขึ้น ผู้คนหันไปใช้รถยนต์ บ้านที่สร้างใหม่จึงหันหน้าออกสู่ถนน ตลาดน้ำหลายแห่งค่อย ๆ ซบเซาลง ปัจจุบันบางชุมชนพยายามฟื้นฟูตลาดน้ำให้เป็นแหล่งท่องเที่ยว เพื่อสร้างรายได้และรักษาวิถีชีวิตดั้งเดิมไว้","table":null,"stem":"ใจความสำคัญของข้อความนี้คือข้อใด","choices":["การคมนาคมที่เปลี่ยนจากทางน้ำเป็นทางบก ทำให้วิถีชีวิตริมน้ำเปลี่ยนแปลงไป","รถยนต์สะดวกกว่าเรือในทุกด้าน","ชาวบ้านริมแม่น้ำเจ้าพระยาไม่ชอบใช้ถนน","ตลาดน้ำเป็นแหล่งท่องเที่ยวที่สำคัญที่สุดของประเทศไทย"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Every sentence links the change from boats to roads with changes in riverside life: houses turned to face roads, floating markets declined, and some are now revived. That cause-and-effect is the main idea; the other statements are not stated or go too far.","th":"ทุกประโยคเชื่อมโยงการเปลี่ยนจากเรือมาใช้ถนนกับการเปลี่ยนแปลงวิถีชีวิตริมน้ำ ทั้งการหันหน้าบ้าน ตลาดน้ำที่ซบเซา และการฟื้นฟูในปัจจุบัน ใจความสำคัญจึงเป็นเรื่องการคมนาคมที่เปลี่ยนไปทำให้วิถีชีวิตริมน้ำเปลี่ยนแปลง ส่วนข้อความอื่นไม่ได้กล่าวไว้หรือสรุปเกินข้อมูล"}}]}},{"exam":"gate","set":2,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 GATE Program — Practice set 2","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 GATE Program — ชุดฝึก 2"},"note":{"en":"40 questions: Mathematics 15, Science 15, English 5, Thai 5. DeepDistrict practice format based on the school's published subjects — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ: คณิตศาสตร์ 15 วิทยาศาสตร์ 15 ภาษาอังกฤษ 5 ภาษาไทย 5 — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ตามวิชาที่โรงเรียนประกาศ ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"subjects":{"math":15,"sci":15,"eng":5,"thai":5},"free":false,"file":"gate-2","sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"จำนวน 5□72 หารด้วย 9 ลงตัว เลขโดดใน □ คือเลขใด","choices":["6","3","0","4"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"A number is divisible by 9 when its digit sum is. 5 + 7 + 2 = 14, and the next multiple of 9 is 18, so the missing digit is 18 − 14 = 4 (5,472 = 9 × 608).","th":"จำนวนที่หารด้วย 9 ลงตัวต้องมีผลบวกของเลขโดดหารด้วย 9 ลงตัว 5 + 7 + 2 = 14 พหุคูณของ 9 ถัดไปคือ 18 จึงต้องเติม 18 − 14 = 4 (5,472 = 9 × 608)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"รถไฟขบวนหนึ่งยาว 200 เมตร แล่นผ่านสะพานยาว 400 เมตร ตั้งแต่หัวรถเริ่มขึ้นสะพานจนท้ายรถพ้นสะพาน ใช้เวลา 30 วินาที รถไฟแล่นด้วยอัตราเร็วกี่กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง","choices":["24","20","48","72"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"To clear the bridge the train travels its own length plus the bridge: 200 + 400 = 600 m in 30 s = 20 m/s. 20 m/s × 3.6 = 72 km/h. (Using only 400 m gives 48 km/h.)","th":"รถไฟต้องเคลื่อนที่ได้ระยะเท่ากับความยาวขบวนบวกความยาวสะพาน 200 + 400 = 600 เมตร ใน 30 วินาที = 20 เมตร/วินาที × 3.6 = 72 กิโลเมตร/ชั่วโมง (ถ้าใช้แค่ 400 เมตร จะได้ 48 ซึ่งผิด)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ABCD เป็นรูปสี่เหลี่ยมผืนผ้า AB = 12 ซม. และ BC = 8 ซม. จุด E เป็นจุดกึ่งกลางของ BC และจุด F เป็นจุดกึ่งกลางของ CD พื้นที่ของรูปสามเหลี่ยม AEF เป็นกี่ตารางเซนติเมตร","choices":["40","48","32","36"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Subtract the three corner triangles from the rectangle (96 cm²): ABE = 12 × 4 ÷ 2 = 24, ECF = 4 × 6 ÷ 2 = 12, ADF = 8 × 6 ÷ 2 = 24. Area AEF = 96 − 24 − 12 − 24 = 36 cm².","th":"นำพื้นที่สี่เหลี่ยมผืนผ้า 96 ตร.ซม. ลบสามเหลี่ยมที่มุมทั้งสาม: ABE = 12 × 4 ÷ 2 = 24, ECF = 4 × 6 ÷ 2 = 12, ADF = 8 × 6 ÷ 2 = 24 พื้นที่ AEF = 96 − 24 − 12 − 24 = 36 ตร.ซม."}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"แก๊สใดที่พืชปล่อยออกมาจากกระบวนการสังเคราะห์ด้วยแสง","choices":["แก๊สไนโตรเจน","แก๊สออกซิเจน","ไอน้ำเท่านั้น","แก๊สคาร์บอนไดออกไซด์"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"In photosynthesis plants use carbon dioxide, water and light energy to make sugar and release oxygen gas.","th":"การสังเคราะห์ด้วยแสง พืชใช้แก๊สคาร์บอนไดออกไซด์ น้ำ และพลังงานแสง สร้างน้ำตาล และปล่อยแก๊สออกซิเจนออกมา"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"การเปลี่ยนแปลงใดเป็นการเปลี่ยนแปลงทางเคมี","choices":["ฉีกกระดาษเป็นชิ้นเล็ก ๆ","น้ำแข็งละลายเป็นน้ำ","ละลายน้ำตาลในน้ำ","ตะปูเหล็กเกิดสนิม"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Rust is a new substance (iron oxide) formed when iron reacts with oxygen and water, so it is a chemical change. Melting, dissolving and tearing change only form or state; no new substance forms.","th":"สนิมเหล็กเป็นสารใหม่ที่เกิดจากเหล็กทำปฏิกิริยากับออกซิเจนและน้ำ จึงเป็นการเปลี่ยนแปลงทางเคมี ส่วนการละลายของน้ำแข็ง การละลายน้ำตาล และการฉีกกระดาษ ไม่เกิดสารใหม่ จึงเป็นการเปลี่ยนแปลงทางกายภาพ"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":{"title":"ผลการทดลองแกว่งลูกตุ้ม","rows":[["การทดลอง","ความยาวเชือก (ซม.)","มวลลูกตุ้ม (g)","คาบ (วินาที)"],["1","25","50","1.0"],["2","25","100","1.0"],["3","100","50","2.0"],["4","100","100","2.0"]]},"stem":"นักเรียนทดลองแกว่งลูกตุ้มแล้วจับเวลาที่ใช้แกว่งครบ 1 รอบ (คาบ) ได้ผลดังตาราง ข้อสรุปใดถูกต้อง","choices":["คาบขึ้นกับมวลของลูกตุ้ม แต่ไม่ขึ้นกับความยาวเชือก","คาบขึ้นกับความยาวเชือก แต่ไม่ขึ้นกับมวลของลูกตุ้ม","เมื่อความยาวเชือกเพิ่มขึ้น 4 เท่า คาบจะเพิ่มขึ้น 4 เท่า","ทั้งมวลและความยาวเชือกมีผลต่อคาบเท่า ๆ กัน"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Trials 1 and 2 (same length, different mass) give the same period, so mass has no effect. Trials 1 and 3 (same mass, length × 4) change the period from 1.0 s to 2.0 s, so length matters — and the period only doubles, not ×4.","th":"การทดลองที่ 1 และ 2 ความยาวเท่ากัน มวลต่างกัน ได้คาบเท่ากัน แสดงว่ามวลไม่มีผล การทดลองที่ 1 และ 3 มวลเท่ากัน ความยาวเพิ่ม 4 เท่า คาบเปลี่ยนจาก 1.0 เป็น 2.0 วินาที แสดงว่าความยาวมีผล และคาบเพิ่มเพียง 2 เท่า ไม่ใช่ 4 เท่า"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct word: There ___ some milk in the fridge.","choices":["is","are","be","have"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Milk is an uncountable noun, so it takes a singular verb: there is some milk.","th":"milk เป็นคำนามนับไม่ได้ จึงใช้กริยาเอกพจน์ there is some milk"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Which word is the opposite of \"ancient\"?","choices":["famous","huge","modern","old"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"\"Ancient\" means very old, from long ago. Its opposite is \"modern\" (new, of the present time). \"Old\" has a similar meaning.","th":"ancient แปลว่า เก่าแก่โบราณ คำตรงข้ามคือ modern (ทันสมัย ปัจจุบัน) ส่วน old มีความหมายใกล้เคียงกัน ไม่ใช่ตรงข้าม"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"h","passage":"Nida wanted to know which kind of bag kept ice frozen the longest. She put the same amount of ice into a paper bag, a plastic bag and a cloth bag, and left them all in the sun. She checked every ten minutes. The ice in the plastic bag melted first, while the ice in the cloth bag lasted the longest. Nida was surprised, because she had expected the plastic bag to win. She decided to repeat the test the next day to make sure her result was not a mistake.","table":null,"stem":"Why did Nida decide to repeat the test the next day?","choices":["Because the ice in the cloth bag never melted.","To check that her result was reliable.","Because she wanted to use more ice.","Because her teacher said the result was wrong."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Nida was surprised by the result and repeated the test \"to make sure her result was not a mistake\" — that is, to check it was reliable. The other reasons are not in the text.","th":"นิดาประหลาดใจกับผลการทดลอง จึงทำซ้ำ \"to make sure her result was not a mistake\" คือเพื่อตรวจสอบว่าผลเชื่อถือได้ เหตุผลอื่นไม่ได้กล่าวไว้ในเรื่อง"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"คำราชาศัพท์ที่ใช้แทนคำว่า \"นอน\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์คือคำใด","choices":["ตรัส","บรรทม","สรง","เสวย"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"For the king, \"to sleep\" is บรรทม. เสวย means to eat, สรง means to bathe, and ตรัส means to speak.","th":"คำว่า \"นอน\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์ใช้ว่า บรรทม ส่วนเสวย แปลว่า กิน สรง แปลว่า อาบน้ำ และตรัส แปลว่า พูด"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"คำใดเป็นคำซ้อน","choices":["รถไฟ","ไม้บรรทัด","บ้านเรือน","น้ำแข็ง"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"บ้านเรือน joins two words with similar meaning (house + house), so it is a คำซ้อน. รถไฟ, น้ำแข็ง and ไม้บรรทัด join words to make a new meaning, so they are คำประสม.","th":"\"บ้านเรือน\" เกิดจากคำที่มีความหมายคล้ายกันมาซ้อนกัน จึงเป็นคำซ้อน ส่วน \"รถไฟ\" \"น้ำแข็ง\" และ \"ไม้บรรทัด\" เป็นคำประสม เพราะนำคำมารวมกันแล้วเกิดความหมายใหม่"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"h","passage":"ผึ้งงานตัวหนึ่งมีชีวิตอยู่เพียงราวหกสัปดาห์ในฤดูที่ต้องทำงานหนัก ตลอดชีวิตมันผลิตน้ำผึ้งได้ไม่ถึงหนึ่งช้อนชา แต่เมื่อผึ้งนับหมื่นตัวในรังช่วยกันทำงานคนละเล็กละน้อย รังผึ้งก็มีน้ำผึ้งสะสมไว้มากพอให้ทั้งรังอยู่รอดผ่านช่วงที่ไม่มีดอกไม้บานได้","table":null,"stem":"ผู้เขียนต้องการสื่อแนวคิดใดมากที่สุด","choices":["ผึ้งงานมีอายุสั้นจึงควรได้รับการคุ้มครอง","น้ำผึ้งเป็นอาหารที่หายากและมีราคาแพง","ความร่วมมือกันของคนจำนวนมาก แม้แต่ละคนทำได้เพียงเล็กน้อย ก็สร้างผลสำเร็จที่ยิ่งใหญ่ได้","ผู้ที่ทำงานหนักมักมีชีวิตสั้น"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The text contrasts how little one bee makes with how much the whole hive stores by working together. The message is that many small efforts combined achieve something great.","th":"ข้อความเปรียบเทียบว่าผึ้งตัวเดียวผลิตน้ำผึ้งได้น้อยมาก แต่เมื่อทั้งรังช่วยกันจึงมีน้ำผึ้งพอให้ทั้งรังอยู่รอด แนวคิดที่ผู้เขียนต้องการสื่อคือ ความร่วมมือกันของคนจำนวนมาก แม้แต่ละคนทำได้เพียงเล็กน้อย ก็สร้างผลสำเร็จที่ยิ่งใหญ่ได้"}}]}},{"exam":"gate","set":3,"title":{"en":"Suankularb M.1 GATE Program — Practice set 3","th":"สวนกุหลาบ ม.1 GATE Program — ชุดฝึก 3"},"note":{"en":"40 questions: Mathematics 15, Science 15, English 5, Thai 5. DeepDistrict practice format based on the school's published subjects — not an official or past paper.","th":"40 ข้อ: คณิตศาสตร์ 15 วิทยาศาสตร์ 15 ภาษาอังกฤษ 5 ภาษาไทย 5 — แบบฝึกของ DeepDistrict ตามวิชาที่โรงเรียนประกาศ ไม่ใช่ข้อสอบจริงหรือข้อสอบเก่า"},"minutes":90,"kinds":{"m1":40},"subjects":{"math":15,"sci":15,"eng":5,"thai":5},"free":false,"file":"gate-3","sample":{"questions":[{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"48 ÷ 4 × 3 − 2² × 5 มีค่าเท่าใด","choices":["4","160","16","26"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"Powers first: 2² = 4. Then × and ÷ from left to right: 48 ÷ 4 × 3 = 36 and 4 × 5 = 20. Finally 36 − 20 = 16. (Doing 4 × 3 first gives 48 ÷ 12 and leads to a wrong answer.)","th":"คิดเลขยกกำลังก่อน 2² = 4 แล้วคูณหารจากซ้ายไปขวา 48 ÷ 4 × 3 = 36 และ 4 × 5 = 20 สุดท้าย 36 − 20 = 16 (ถ้าคูณ 4 × 3 ก่อนจะได้ 48 ÷ 12 ซึ่งผิดลำดับ)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ชายสองคนอยู่ห่างกัน 36 กิโลเมตร เดินเข้าหากันด้วยอัตราเร็ว 5 และ 7 กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง สุนัขตัวหนึ่งวิ่งกลับไปกลับมาระหว่างชายทั้งสองด้วยอัตราเร็ว 15 กิโลเมตรต่อชั่วโมง ตั้งแต่เริ่มเดินจนทั้งสองพบกัน สุนัขวิ่งได้ระยะทางทั้งหมดกี่กิโลเมตร","choices":["45","30","36","54"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The men close the gap at 5 + 7 = 12 km/h, so they meet after 36 ÷ 12 = 3 hours. The dog runs for those same 3 hours: 15 × 3 = 45 km. No need to follow each back-and-forth trip.","th":"ทั้งสองเดินเข้าหากันด้วยอัตราเร็วรวม 5 + 7 = 12 กม./ชม. จึงพบกันหลัง 36 ÷ 12 = 3 ชั่วโมง สุนัขวิ่งตลอด 3 ชั่วโมงนั้น ระยะทาง = 15 × 3 = 45 กม. ไม่ต้องคิดทีละเที่ยว"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"math","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ลูกบาศก์ไม้ยาวด้านละ 6 ซม. ทาสีแดงทุกด้าน แล้วตัดเป็นลูกบาศก์เล็กยาวด้านละ 1 ซม. ทั้งหมด จะมีลูกบาศก์เล็กที่ถูกทาสีแดงเพียง 2 ด้านกี่ลูก","choices":["48","96","8","64"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Cubes with exactly two red faces lie along the 12 edges but not at the corners: each edge has 6 − 2 = 4 such cubes, so 12 × 4 = 48. (96 have one red face, 64 have none, 8 corners have three.)","th":"ลูกบาศก์เล็กที่มีสีสองด้านอยู่ตามขอบ 12 เส้น ยกเว้นที่มุม ขอบละ 6 − 2 = 4 ลูก รวม 12 × 4 = 48 ลูก (สีด้านเดียวมี 96 ลูก ไม่มีสีเลย 64 ลูก และที่มุมมีสีสามด้าน 8 ลูก)"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ส่วนใดของเซลล์ทำหน้าที่ควบคุมการทำงานของเซลล์และเก็บสารพันธุกรรม","choices":["แวคิวโอล","นิวเคลียส","เยื่อหุ้มเซลล์","ไซโทพลาซึม"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The nucleus contains the genetic material (DNA) and controls the cell's activities. The cell membrane controls what enters and leaves; the cytoplasm and vacuole do not control the cell.","th":"นิวเคลียสเก็บสารพันธุกรรม (DNA) และควบคุมการทำงานของเซลล์ เยื่อหุ้มเซลล์ควบคุมการเข้าออกของสาร ส่วนไซโทพลาซึมและแวคิวโอลไม่ได้ทำหน้าที่ควบคุมเซลล์"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"ตะโกนหน้าหน้าผาแล้วได้ยินเสียงสะท้อนกลับมาหลังจากตะโกน 4 วินาที ถ้าอัตราเร็วเสียงในอากาศเท่ากับ 340 เมตรต่อวินาที หน้าผาอยู่ห่างออกไปกี่เมตร","choices":["1360","340","680","85"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"In 4 s the sound goes to the cliff and back: 340 × 4 = 1,360 m in total. The cliff is half of that, 680 m away.","th":"ใน 4 วินาที เสียงเดินทางไปถึงหน้าผาแล้วสะท้อนกลับ รวม 340 × 4 = 1,360 เมตร หน้าผาจึงอยู่ห่างครึ่งหนึ่ง คือ 680 เมตร"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"sci","difficulty":"h","passage":"","table":{"title":"ความหนาแน่นของของเหลว","rows":[["ของเหลว","ความหนาแน่น (g/cm³)"],["น้ำมันพืช","0.92"],["น้ำ","1.00"],["น้ำเชื่อมเข้มข้น","1.40"],["สารละลาย X","1.80"]]},"stem":"ก้อนวัสดุรูปสี่เหลี่ยมมุมฉากขนาด 4 × 5 × 10 ซม. มีมวล 300 กรัม เมื่อนำไปใส่ในของเหลวแต่ละชนิดในตาราง ก้อนวัสดุนี้จะลอยในของเหลวใด","choices":["สารละลาย X","น้ำเชื่อมเข้มข้น","น้ำมันพืช","น้ำ"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Volume = 4 × 5 × 10 = 200 cm³, so density = 300 ÷ 200 = 1.5 g/cm³. It floats only in a liquid denser than 1.5 g/cm³: liquid X (1.80). It sinks in oil, water and syrup (1.40).","th":"ปริมาตร = 4 × 5 × 10 = 200 ลบ.ซม. ความหนาแน่น = 300 ÷ 200 = 1.5 g/cm³ จะลอยได้เฉพาะในของเหลวที่หนาแน่นกว่า 1.5 คือสารละลาย X (1.80) ส่วนน้ำมันพืช น้ำ และน้ำเชื่อมเข้มข้น (1.40) หนาแน่นน้อยกว่า วัสดุจึงจม"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the correct word: Our school sports day is ___ Friday.","choices":["by","at","on","in"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"We use \"on\" with days and dates: on Friday, on 5 May. \"In\" is for months and years, \"at\" for clock times.","th":"ใช้ on กับวันและวันที่ เช่น on Friday ส่วน in ใช้กับเดือนและปี และ at ใช้กับเวลา"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"Choose the word closest in meaning to \"enormous\" in this sentence: The elephant was enormous.","choices":["tiny","huge","friendly","noisy"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"\"Enormous\" means extremely big, the same as \"huge\". \"Tiny\" is the opposite.","th":"enormous แปลว่า ใหญ่มาก มีความหมายเดียวกับ huge ส่วน tiny มีความหมายตรงข้าม"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"eng","difficulty":"h","passage":"Dear parents,\nThe school trip to the Science Museum will now take place on Friday 14 November instead of Thursday 13 November, because the museum is closed for repairs on Thursday. Buses will leave at 7.30 a.m., half an hour earlier than planned, so that students can join the planetarium show at 9.00. Students should bring a packed lunch, as the museum café will not be open. Please return the signed form by Monday 10 November.","table":null,"stem":"According to the notice, what time were the buses first planned to leave?","choices":["7.30 a.m.","8.30 a.m.","8.00 a.m.","9.00 a.m."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The buses will now leave at 7.30 a.m., \"half an hour earlier than planned\". So the original plan was half an hour later: 8.00 a.m. 9.00 is the planetarium show.","th":"ประกาศบอกว่ารถออก 7.30 น. ซึ่ง \"เร็วกว่าที่วางแผนไว้ครึ่งชั่วโมง\" เวลาเดิมจึงช้ากว่าครึ่งชั่วโมง คือ 8.00 น. ส่วน 9.00 น. เป็นเวลาการแสดงท้องฟ้าจำลอง"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"e","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"คำราชาศัพท์ที่ใช้แทนคำว่า \"ป่วย\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์คือคำใด","choices":["บรรทม","ประชวร","เสด็จ","ประทับ"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"For the king, \"to be ill\" is ประชวร. ประทับ means to sit or stay, เสด็จ means to go, and บรรทม means to sleep.","th":"คำว่า \"ป่วย\" สำหรับพระมหากษัตริย์ใช้ว่า ประชวร ส่วนประทับ แปลว่า นั่งหรืออยู่ เสด็จ แปลว่า ไป และบรรทม แปลว่า นอน"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"m","passage":"","table":null,"stem":"\"แม่ซื้อร่มมาให้ฉัน 2 ___\" ควรเติมคำลักษณนามใด","choices":["อัน","ด้าม","คัน","เล่ม"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The classifier for umbrellas is คัน (as for cars and spoons with handles). ด้าม is used for pens, and เล่ม for books and knives.","th":"ลักษณนามของร่มคือ \"คัน\" ส่วน \"ด้าม\" ใช้กับปากกา และ \"เล่ม\" ใช้กับหนังสือหรือมีด"}},{"kind":"m1","program":"gate","subject":"thai","difficulty":"h","passage":"หลายคนเชื่อว่าการอ่านหนังสือให้ได้มากเล่มที่สุดคือหนทางสู่ความรู้ แต่การอ่านเร็ว ๆ โดยไม่หยุดคิดก็เหมือนการเทน้ำลงบนหิน น้ำไหลผ่านไปหมดโดยไม่ซึมลงไปเลย ผู้อ่านที่ดีจึงควรอ่านอย่างช้าพอที่จะตั้งคำถาม โต้แย้ง และเชื่อมโยงสิ่งที่อ่านกับประสบการณ์ของตน แม้จะอ่านได้น้อยเล่มกว่า แต่ความรู้ที่ได้จะติดตัวไปนาน","table":null,"stem":"ผู้เขียนใช้การเปรียบเทียบ \"การเทน้ำลงบนหิน\" เพื่อสื่อความหมายใด","choices":["ผู้อ่านควรอ่านหนังสือให้ได้มากเล่มที่สุด","การอ่านหนังสือมากเกินไปทำให้เหนื่อยล้า","หนังสือบางเล่มยากเกินกว่าจะเข้าใจได้","การอ่านโดยไม่คิดตาม ทำให้ความรู้ไม่ติดอยู่ในตัวผู้อ่าน"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Water poured on rock runs off without soaking in. The writer compares this to reading fast without thinking: the knowledge does not stay with the reader. The text actually argues against reading as many books as possible.","th":"น้ำที่เทลงบนหินไหลผ่านไปโดยไม่ซึมลงไป ผู้เขียนเปรียบกับการอ่านเร็ว ๆ โดยไม่คิดตาม ความรู้จึงไม่ติดอยู่กับผู้อ่าน และข้อความนี้แย้งความเชื่อเรื่องการอ่านให้ได้มากเล่มที่สุด"}}]}}];
